2c:["$","p","4",{"children":"Every required field is a small tax on the person entering data. Ask for the minimum needed to act on a record and to report on the pipeline. You can add fields later. Removing the habit of skipping them is much harder."}]
2d:["$","h2","5",{"children":"Clean the data before it moves"}]
2e:["$","p","6",{"children":"Migrating years of duplicated, half-complete contacts into a new system makes the new system feel old on day one. Deduplicate, archive what is stale and import only what someone would reasonably use."}]
2f:["$","h2","7",{"children":"Make it the easiest way to work"}]
30:["$","ul","8",{"children":[["$","li","Connect email, phone and web forms so records create themselves.",{"children":"Connect email, phone and web forms so records create themselves."}],["$","li","Automate reminders so the system helps people, instead of only asking things of them.",{"children":"Automate reminders so the system helps people, instead of only asking things of them."}],["$","li","Run reviews and meetings from the CRM, so that being up to date is visibly useful.",{"children":"Run reviews and meetings from the CRM, so that being up to date is visibly useful."}]]}]
31:["$","p","9",{"children":"When the CRM saves people effort, adoption follows. When it feels like reporting for management, it quietly empties."}]
